@page "/legacy-host"
@using Crest.Admin.Components.Admin

@* Phase 8: the server-side (SSR/InteractiveServer) document host for admin URLs that
   are NOT Crest Blazor pages - BlazorAdminThemeMiddleware rewrites those requests to
   this route instead of index-html-serving them like the old WASM shell did. The
   browser URL stays the original admin path, so LegacyAdminFrame (which reads
   NavigationManager.Uri) iframes the right legacy Orchard page, and once the client
   Router takes over it resolves the same URL to its NotFound branch -> the same
   LegacyAdminFrame. Listed in AdminRoutes' shell-less set: LegacyAdminFrame brings
   its own CrestAppContainer, so the Found-branch wrapper would double-wrap it. *@

<LegacyAdminFrame />
